<article><h1>Province expands heat pump rebate to renters</h1>
<p>The Example Province energy ministry said on November 12, 2026 that renters can now apply for the heat pump rebate. Until now, only owners could apply for it.</p>
<p>The rebate covers up to $5,000 of the cost of a new heat pump. A renter needs written consent from the property owner before the installation starts.</p>
<p>Energy Minister Robin Sample said the change could reach about 40,000 more households across the province. Applications open on December 1, 2026 through the provincial portal.</p>
<p>The ministry also said the program budget grows to $120 million for the 2027 fiscal year.</p>
